  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Battles will enter with double the normal number of defense counters.",
      "oracle_id": "01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Doubling Season affects permanents that enter with counters.",
      "oracle_id": "01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Everything that is specified by the effect creating the original token or tokens will also be true about the additional token or tokens created by Doubling Season's replacement effect. For example, if an effect tells you to create a token \"tapped and attacking,\" the additional tokens will also be tapped and attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If there are two Doubling Seasons on the battlefield, then the number of tokens or counters is four times the original number. If there are three on the battlefield, then the number of tokens or counters is eight times the original number, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Planeswalkers will enter with double the normal number of loyalty counters. However, if you activate an ability whose cost has you put loyalty counters on a planeswalker, the number you put on isn't doubled. This is because those counters are put on as a cost, not as an effect.",
      "oracle_id": "01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Valduk leaves the battlefield after its ability has resolved, the tokens are still exiled at the beginning of the next end step.",
      "oracle_id": "102b0a65-f2e0-4ef3-a9dc-4a85557b852e",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Valduk leaves the battlefield after its ability has triggered but before it resolves, use the number of Auras and Equipment that were last attached to it before it left the battlefield to determine how many tokens to create.",
      "oracle_id": "102b0a65-f2e0-4ef3-a9dc-4a85557b852e",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Valduk counts all Auras and Equipment attached to it, not only Auras and Equipment you control.",
      "oracle_id": "102b0a65-f2e0-4ef3-a9dc-4a85557b852e",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although the token you created is put onto the battlefield attacking, it was never declared as an attacking creature. Abilities that trigger whenever a creature attacks won\u2019t trigger when that creature enters attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "1972e0db-e595-4ec2-b97c-902561bb275b",
      "published_at": "2025-07-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You choose the player, planeswalker, or battle the token is attacking. It doesn\u2019t have to be the same player, planeswalker, or battle that Kavaron Harrier or any other attacking creatures are attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "1972e0db-e595-4ec2-b97c-902561bb275b",
      "published_at": "2025-07-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A landfall ability doesn't trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.",
      "oracle_id": "36d1a46e-44ac-4a65-a93c-8d6ab5c31cbf",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A landfall ability triggers whenever a land you control enters for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.",
      "oracle_id": "36d1a46e-44ac-4a65-a93c-8d6ab5c31cbf",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Whenever a land you control enters, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them \u00a0\u00a0on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve (As a result, you can have those abilities resolve in the order of your choosing.).",
      "oracle_id": "36d1a46e-44ac-4a65-a93c-8d6ab5c31cbf",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although the token created is an attacking creature, it was never declared as an attacking creature. This means that abilities that trigger whenever a creature attacks won't trigger when it enters the battlefield attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "411cf990-972c-4ee3-9ae4-98602f269407",
      "published_at": "2022-06-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While resolving Carefree Swinemaster's triggered ability, you can't pay the cost multiple times to create more than one token.",
      "oracle_id": "411cf990-972c-4ee3-9ae4-98602f269407",
      "published_at": "2022-06-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You choose which player or planeswalker is being attacked by the Boar token as it enters the battlefield. It doesn't have to be the same player or planeswalker that Carefree Swinemaster is attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "411cf990-972c-4ee3-9ae4-98602f269407",
      "published_at": "2022-06-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the ability is activated after the current turn's End step has begun, the tokens won't be exiled until the next turn's End step.",
      "oracle_id": "4234f07e-583f-40db-8b47-7e16c7316e19",
      "published_at": "2008-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The enchanted creature's power is checked at the time the ability resolves. If the enchanted creature has left the battlefield by then, its last known information is used.",
      "oracle_id": "4234f07e-583f-40db-8b47-7e16c7316e19",
      "published_at": "2008-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The tokens will be exiled in the End step even if Elemental Mastery or the enchanted creature has left the battlefield by then.",
      "oracle_id": "4234f07e-583f-40db-8b47-7e16c7316e19",
      "published_at": "2008-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although the tokens enter the battlefield attacking, they were never declared as attacking creatures. Abilities that trigger whenever a creature attacks won't trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "4a3a25ae-61f5-4bcd-ae3d-4b31feaa83d8",
      "published_at": "2022-10-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For the triggered ability, you declare which player or planeswalker the token is attacking as you put it onto the battlefield. It doesn't have to be the same player or planeswalker the equipped creature is attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "4a3a25ae-61f5-4bcd-ae3d-4b31feaa83d8",
      "published_at": "2022-10-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The token enters attacking. It doesn't trigger \"when a creature attacks\" triggers and is not subject to restrictions on declaring attackers.",
      "oracle_id": "d311154b-4742-49e5-9b65-4de2d3e0d50b",
      "published_at": "2007-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You choose which player or planeswalker the token is attacking. It doesn't have to attack the same player or planeswalker as the creature that caused the ability to trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "d311154b-4742-49e5-9b65-4de2d3e0d50b",
      "published_at": "2007-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Kindred is a card type that allows noncreature cards to have creature types. For example, Echoes of Eternity is an Eldrazi (although not a creature) while on the battlefield and an Eldrazi card (although not a creature card) in zones other than the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "d311154b-4742-49e5-9b65-4de2d3e0d50b",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This cards was originally printed with the \"tribal\" card type. That card type has been replaced with \"kindred\". This change does not affect the gameplay function of this card.",
      "oracle_id": "d311154b-4742-49e5-9b65-4de2d3e0d50b",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While it appears only on cards that already have other card types, kindred is a card type and will be counted by effects that refer to the number of card types among cards in a zone.",
      "oracle_id": "d311154b-4742-49e5-9b65-4de2d3e0d50b",
      "published_at": "2024-06-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Manaform Hellkite's triggered ability looks at the mana that was actually spent to cast the spell, which may be different than the mana cost of that spell. For example, if you cast a noncreature spell without paying its mana cost, this ability creates a 0/0 Dragon Illusion token. In most cases, such a creature would immediately be put into your graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "f426aa1a-e1dc-4563-b450-2e23d6bd980b",
      "published_at": "2021-11-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
